{"name":"Royal Decree","hex":"#403547","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"royal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to a monarch or his (or her) family.","Having the air or demeanour of a monarch; illustrious; magnanimous; of more than common size or excellence."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A royal person; a member of a royal family.","A standard size of printing paper, measuring 25 by 20 inches."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/royal"},{"term":"decree","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edict or law.","The judicial decision in a litigated cause rendered by a court of equity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To command, especially by a decree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Decree","blocks":[{"text":"A decree is a legal proclamation, usually issued by a head of state, judge, royal figure, or other relevant authorities, according to certain procedures. These procedures are usually defined by the constitution, legislative laws, or customary laws of a government."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Casimir_The_Great_Decree.jpg/330px-Casimir_The_Great_Decree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decree","wikidata":"Q2571972"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Ali_Khamenei_first_presidency_decree_by_Rohullah_Khomeini_%283%29.jpg/500px-Ali_Khamenei_first_presidency_decree_by_Rohullah_Khomeini_%283%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Ali_Khamenei_first_presidency_decree_by_Rohullah_Khomeini_%283%29.jpg/1280px-Ali_Khamenei_first_presidency_decree_by_Rohullah_Khomeini_%283%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w